Package: mortensor
Title: Flexible Mortality Forecasting Across Data Granularities
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R:
    person("Karl", "Emmert-Fees", email = "karl.emmert-fees@tum.de",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Tools to combine mortality and population data observed at
    different granularities (age groups, open age intervals, periods,
    population strata and causes) and to build probabilistic mortality
    forecasts from interchangeable parts: harmonisation and ungrouping with the
    penalized composite link model; models implemented directly (random walk
    with drift, Lee-Carter, Li-Lee, Tucker3) or wrapped from 'demography',
    'StMoMo', 'StanMoMo', 'bamp' and 'forecast' behind one interface; ensembles of any
    combination of them; coherent forecasts of totals and their parts;
    honest rolling-origin backtests with proper scoring rules; and life
    tables computed from simulated paths.
    Experimental software written largely with AI coding assistants
    ("vibe-coded"); use at your own risk and check results independently.
